<title>HONG KONG: Styland posts sharp rise in interim net.</title>
<headline>Styland posts sharp rise in interim net.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended September 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   0.05  vs 0.0009 (see note)</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    nil   vs nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil   vs 11.03</p>
<p>    Net			    0.503 vs 0.006</p>
<p>    Turnover		     87.61 vs 26.56</p>
<p>    Company name		 Styland Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  N/A</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - Styland is a holding company for a group of garment and consumer electronics firms. The company is proposing a bonus issue of one warrant for every five shares held. Each warrant entitles holder the rights to subscribe one new company share at HK$0.30 per share before maturity on February 18, 1998.</p>
<p>Share earnings have been adjusted for the rights issue of 450.86 million shares during the fiscal year ended March 31, 1996.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
